  "notes": "Composed of {発|はつ} (emit, produce) + {芽|が} (bud, sprout). Used in gardening, agriculture, and biology contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {発芽|はつが}{率|りつ}: germination rate\n- {発芽|はつが}{玄米|げんまい}: germinated brown rice (a health food)\n- {発芽|はつが}{条件|じょうけん}: germination conditions\n- {発芽|はつが}する: to germinate, to sprout\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {芽|め}が{出|で}る: to sprout (more colloquial; also used figuratively for \"showing promise\")\n- {発根|はっこん}: root emergence (a later stage of growth)\n\nUSAGE:\nThe three conditions for germination are commonly taught as {水|みず} (water), {温度|おんど} (temperature), and {空気|くうき} (air).",
